course: dictionary
lesson: 14489
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and «paving» is one of these words. Its noun meaning is flat stones, bricks or slabs laid on the ground. Its verb meaning is the act of covering ground with them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning is in use.
explain: «The workmen spent all morning paving the car park.» Here paving is an action. Ask yourself: is someone doing something, or is it a thing? Someone is doing it, so it means covering the ground with stones.
explain: «The old paving was cracked, so Sam nearly tripped.» Here paving is a thing, the flat stones under his feet. Cracked and tripped are the clues. Test your meaning: "The old stones were cracked, so Sam nearly tripped" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Sometimes the word is used in a special phrase. «Her kind letter is paving the way for a new friendship.» Paving the way has nothing to do with stones. It means making it easier for something to happen later. Context clues help you see this.
fact: Paving is flat stones, bricks or slabs laid on the ground to make a path, patio or pavement.
fact: Paving can also mean the act of covering ground with these stones.
fact: «Paving the way» means making it easier for something to happen later.
fact: In British and Irish English, the footpath beside a road is the pavement; Americans call it the sidewalk.
fact: Cracked or uneven paving can make people trip, so always watch where you walk.
exercise: «The workmen spent all morning paving the car park.» What does paving mean here? | Painting the walls | Digging a deep hole | Walking very slowly | *Covering the ground with stones
exercise: «The cracked paving outside school made Ella trip.» What is the paving in this sentence? | A loud noise | A school rule | A type of tree | *Flat stones on the ground
exercise: «Her kind letter is paving the way for a new friendship.» What does paving the way mean? | Writing a letter quickly | Being very tired after a long day | Laying stones across a river | *Making it easier for something to happen later
test: In British English, what is the footpath beside a road called? | Gravel drive | *Pavement | Runway | Sidewalk, the American word
test: «The shop sold paving for the patio.» What does paving mean here? | Waiting patiently | Selling things in a shop | Covering the ground with stones, as an action | *Flat slabs laid on the ground
exam: Which sentence uses paving as an action? | *«The team is paving the new lane with bricks.» | «The paving was smooth and grey.» | «We saw paving stones by the river.» | «The crazy paving looked lovely.»
